-- action-filters,entity-actions,roles,entity-permissions,authorization-roles` (MJ CLI 6.2.1) against
-- a database built from migrations ONLY: MJ core v6.2.1, the released sibling apps, then this app's
-- migrations at `next`. Those folders hold every metadata change since v5.50.2. Push result:
-- 14 created, 10 updated, 0 errors; 8 of the updates change no value and write no SQL.
--
-- CREATED (create-only: each is guarded on its ID or its natural key, and the push log's update
-- branches are cut, so a host that already has the row keeps its own values):
--   Roles (3)              Senior Finance (AR), CFO, CEO Approver. Guard: ID or Name.
--   Entity permissions (5) Entitlement Access Overrides for Account Director, Finance, Senior
--                          Finance (AR), CFO and CEO Approver (create, read, update; no delete).
--                          Guard: ID or (EntityID, RoleID).
--   Authorization role (1) Senior Finance (AR) on MJ.BizApps.Orders.Access.Override (Allow).
--                          Guard: ID or (AuthorizationID, RoleID).
--   Application settings   BillComCreateCustomerOnSend (true), BillComInvoiceReadyNotifyRole (empty),
--   (3)                    BillComInvoiceReadyWebhookURL (empty). Guard: ID or (ApplicationID, Name).
--   Action filter (1)      "Order Status Changed To Confirmed". MJ: Action Filters has no Name
--                          column, so the guard is ID or UserDescription.
--   Entity action filter   attaches that filter to the Order Headers -> Send Document AfterUpdate
--   (1)                    binding. The binding itself stays Pending. Guard: ID or (EntityActionID,
--                          ActionFilterID); skipped when the binding or the filter is not there.
-- Entities, roles, the authorization and the application resolve on this database by Name, the
-- pinned ID first.
--
-- UPDATED: the type definitions of remote operations Orders.PriceOrder (input and output) and
-- Orders.SpawnRenewals (output), which document the price-order ProductPriceID/Error fields and
-- the renewal prior-line fields. Each resolves by OperationKey, the shipped ID first, and is
-- written only when a definition differs. These are app-owned TypeScript definitions read by
-- callers, not host settings.
--
-- TRANSFORMS: `[${mjSchema}].` -> `[${mjSchema}].` on the SP calls and lookups; string values untouched.
-- Idempotent.
